ASD-STE100 and Simplified Technical English
-------------------------------------------
ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English is a specification published by the
Aerospace, Security and Defence Industries Association of Europe (ASD),
Brussels, Belgium. The specification, including its writing rules, dictionary
and examples, is copyright (c) ASD. "ASD-STE100" is a European Union registered
trade mark of ASD (EU Trade Mark No. 017966390).

This project is independent. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored
by, certified by, or otherwise connected to ASD or the Simplified Technical
English Maintenance Group (STEMG). The names "ASD-STE100" and "Simplified
Technical English" are used only to identify the specification that this tool
checks text against.

This repository does not contain the ASD-STE100 specification, its dictionary,
its rule text or its examples. Each user must get their own copy of the
specification from an official source (https://www.asd-ste100.org or
https://www.asd-europe.org) and build the local data files with
`make dictionary`. The built files (tool/ste_lint/data/dictionary.json and
rules.json) contain ASD material. Do not commit, publish or redistribute them.

No compliance claim
-------------------
ste-lint is an aid for writers who already know ASD-STE100. A clean result
does not mean that a text complies with ASD-STE100, and the tool does not
check every rule. Rule numbers and short rule summaries in this repository are
written by the project to identify rules; they are not the official rule text.

Third-party software
--------------------
ste-lint depends on spaCy and its en_core_web_sm model, pdfplumber, Typer,
Rich and PyYAML. These are installed from their own distribution channels at
setup time under their own licences; none of them is bundled here.
